From 7dddfd9e24e84378fe24008fa129a7a8c6d4b77e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:04:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] action: Adds workspace-by-number actions, and
 WindowToggleShaded.

Window Maker binds Alt+1 ... Alt+0 to "Switch to workspace N" by default
(Workspace1Key ... Workspace10Key), offers "Move window to workspace N"
(MoveToWorkspace1Key ...), and a ShadeKey that toggles the shade. wlmaker
only had next/previous, and WindowShade/WindowUnshade.

WorkspaceSwitchTo and WindowToWorkspace take the workspace's number,
counting from 1, as argument; a number beyond the existing workspaces does
nothing. WindowToggleShaded shades or unshades the active window:

    "Alt+1" = (WorkspaceSwitchTo, "1");
    "Shift+Alt+1" = (WindowToWorkspace, "1");
    "Logo+S" = WindowToggleShaded;

The toolkit gets wlmtk_desktop_get_workspace_at() and
wlmtk_desktop_switch_to_workspace_at().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
